data.content:
## What breaks in .NET 11

In .NET 11 / EF Core 11, the **sync-over-async opt-in for the Cosmos DB provider is removed entirely**. The temporary compatibility switch (e.g., `EnableSyncOverAsync()`) that you configured in .NET 10 no longer exists.

Every synchronous LINQ operator on the Cosmos provider now throws `InvalidOperationException` at runtime with **no workaround**:

| Broken call | Async replacement |
|---|---|
| `.ToList()` | `.ToListAsync()` |
| `.First(...)` | `.FirstAsync(...)` |
| `.Count()` | `.CountAsync()` |
| `.SaveChanges()` | `.SaveChangesAsync()` |

## Required fix

Convert the repository to async:

```csharp
public class ProductRepository
{
    private readonly CosmosDbContext _context;

    public async Task<List<Product>> GetAllAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.ToListAsync();
    }

    public async Task<Product> GetByIdAsync(int id)
    {
        return await _context.Products.FirstAsync(p => p.Id == id);
    }

    public async Task<int> GetCountAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.CountAsync();
    }

    public async Task SaveAsync(Product product)
    {
        _context.Products.Add(product);
        await _context.SaveChangesAsync();
    }
}
```

This will cascade — all callers up the chain must also become `async`/`await`. The Cosmos provider was always async-only internally; .NET 11 simply removes the last escape hatch.
